{"name":"Night Out","hex":"#656a6e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night out","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Going away from one's usual residence for an entire night, and returning the next day.","Spending the evening away from one's usual residence. The phrase typically implies going to a bar or restaurant, going to watch entertainment, or other types of nightlife."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night_out"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night Out (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Out is a 1989 Australian drama film directed by Lawrence Johnston. It is about the consequences of a gay bashing. Johnston made it as his graduating work for his Swinburne Film and Television School studies. It was screened in the Un Certain Regard section at the 1990 Cannes Film Festival."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Out_(film)","wikidata":"Q7033387"},{"title":"Night Out (The Office)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Night Out\" is the fifteenth episode of the fourth season of the American comedy television series The Office and the show's sixty-eighth episode overall. The episode was written by Mindy Kaling and directed by Ken Whittingham. It first aired in the United States on April 24, 2008 on NBC. \"Night Out\" was viewed by a measured audience of over 7.5 million people, bringing in the lowest number of estimated viewers that The Office received among 12 episodes. \"Night Out\" received mixed reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a2/Nightout2.jpg/330px-Nightout2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Out_(The_Office)","wikidata":"Q7033383"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Wga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG/500px-Wga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Wga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG/1280px-Wga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Wga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG/500px-Wga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Writers Guild of America was on strike for 100 days, causing production of The Office to go on hiatus for four months.[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWga_rally_-_ave_stars_-_crossing_street.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Variable spellings of night in a Middle English poem:\n\nÞu sittest a dai & fliȝst a niȝt (top)\nÞu sittest a day and flyhst a niht (bottom)\n'You sit by day and fly by night'\n\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOwl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/1280px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Day and night during the winter solstice in the northern hemisphere","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/500px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/1280px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org